]"],"review_comment":["Can we just use `SortedSetDocValues` here directly instead of using an additional layer of abstraction? \r\n\r\nFor example in `DocValuesSortedKeyedValues` we directly sorted set doc values instead of `DocValuesFieldValues` as an intermediate interface. \r\n","Do we need the `DocValuesFieldValues` interface at all? It is either no value or uses `SortedSetDocValues`. Maybe we always use `SortedSetDocValues` directly and in case of no value it is null?","I was actually looking at that too. I believe we can\u0027t directly use `SortedSetDocValues` because when there is no doc values, it contains an empty singleton which we don\u0027t expect. We could just set it to null indeed.","So `FlattenedFieldDocValuesLoader` also tracks if current document has doc values and i think inlining all this logic into `FlattenedSortedSetDocValuesSyntheticFieldLoader` reduces readability quite a bit. I\u0027ll keep this as is."],"path":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/flattened/FlattenedSortedSetDocValuesSyntheticFieldLoader.java","id":37456,"created_at":"2024-09-25T09:36:38Z","original_position":23,"side":"RIGHT","position":23,"submitted_on_commit":"b552b451084124d5229b56d6b182dda9480b8cb5","diff_hunk":"@@ -13,27 +13,43 @@\n import org.apache.lucene.index.LeafReader;\n import org.apache.lucene.index.SortedSetDocValues;\n import org.apache.lucene.util.BytesRef;\n+import org.elasticsearch.core.Nullable;\n import org.elasticsearch.index.mapper.SourceLoader;\n import org.elasticsearch.xcontent.XContentBuilder;\n \n import java.io.IOException;\n+import java.util.ArrayList;\n+import java.util.List;\n+import java.util.Map;\n+import java.util.TreeSet;\n+import java.util.stream.Stream;\n \n-public class FlattenedSortedSetDocValuesSyntheticFieldLoader extends SourceLoader.DocValuesBasedSyntheticFieldLoader {\n-    private DocValuesFieldValues docValues \u003d NO_VALUES;\n+public class FlattenedSortedSetDocValuesSyntheticFieldLoader implements SourceLoade